WHAT THIS LICENCE COVERS AND DOES NOT COVER

The licence applies to ORA's compilation, harmonisation and structuring of
published values. It grants no rights in the original publications, which
remain under their publishers' terms. Each record identifies its source
publication in the source.citation and source.doi fields (in corpus.csv,
the citation and doi columns).

ATTRIBUTION

When you reuse or redistribute the dataset, or any subset of it, cite both:

  1. This dataset:
     Satoru / DigiShield Labs. ORA: Organic Residue Archive.
     https://github.com/satoru-bio/ORA

  2. The original study for every record you use, as given in that record's
     source.citation and source.doi fields.

Per-record attribution is part of how the dataset is meant to be used. A
subset drawn from a single study still requires a citation of that study.
